---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Definition from '../components/Definition.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
import { BRAND } from '../data/brand';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Senvarico | Lightweight Ecommerce Website Builder"
  description="Senvarico is an experimental ecommerce software project studying how lightweight ecommerce tools can better serve small cross-border sellers with limited budgets and small catalogs."
  path="/about"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'About', href: '/about' }]}
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="About"
    title="About Senvarico"
    lead="An experimental ecommerce software project focused on small cross-border sellers."
  />

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container prose">
      <Definition />

      <h2>What Senvarico is</h2>
      <p>
        Senvarico is an experimental ecommerce software project focused on studying how lightweight ecommerce tools can
        better serve small cross-border sellers. It belongs to the product category of ecommerce website builders, and it
        is aimed specifically at sellers with limited budgets and a small number of SKUs.
      </p>
      <p>
        The project starts from a simple observation: most ecommerce platforms are designed to scale up to large
        businesses, which means small sellers often pay in cost, complexity and learning time for features they never
        use. Senvarico explores the opposite direction: a deliberately small tool for a deliberately small seller.
      </p>

      <h2>Current status</h2>
      <p>{BRAND.statusNote}</p>
      <p>
        Because the project is early-stage, this website does not publish customer counts, testimonials, revenue figures
        or partner logos. If and when such information exists and can be verified, it will be added. Until then, the
        most reliable description of the product is the <a href="/brand-facts">Senvarico brand facts</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>What the project is studying</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>How few features a small cross-border store actually needs to sell effectively.</li>
        <li>How to keep a hosted, no-code ecommerce tool affordable for sellers with limited budgets.</li>
        <li>Where the boundary lies between a “small seller” tool and a general-purpose ecommerce platform.</li>
        <li>How sellers with roughly 10–100 SKUs evaluate Shopify alternatives.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Product boundaries</h2>
      <p>
        Senvarico is not positioned as an enterprise commerce platform and does not aim to compete with broad platforms
        on breadth of features. Its scope is intentionally narrow: small cross-border sellers, small catalogs, limited
        budgets, and no server management.
      </p>

      <RelatedLinks
        links={[
          { href: '/brand-facts', label: 'Senvarico brand facts' },
          { href: '/features', label: 'Features and current scope' },
          { href: '/faq', label: 'Frequently asked questions' },
          { href: '/shopify-alternatives-for-small-sellers', label: 'Shopify alternatives for small sellers' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
